// expect-error: NITPICK-ASSIGN-005
// expect-error-at: 2096:29
mod:assignment_target_runs_before_its_value;
// AN ASSIGNMENT'S TARGET RUNS BEFORE ITS VALUE, AND THE STORE AFTER BOTH (`emit_assign`: `addr_of`, then the value, then the store; DEF-571, landing 177d2b2).
// A jump in the target leaves with nothing the value did (`oe_*_p`, `oh_field_tgt_p`), a jump in the value with what the target did (`og_*`, `oh_field_tgt2_g`). What's unassigned at the target is
// refused there (`oi1`, `oi3`, `wa2`, `oi20`, `oi23`, `oi14` once if it was gone already), a test in the value refines nothing in the target (`oi2`, `wa3`), and a seal in the target or the value stands at the store (`oi11`, `oi7`).
// WHILE THE VALUE RUNS, THE NAMES THE TARGET READ STAND STILL, each refused where the value does it. A move or a free is MOVE-001 or MOVE-002 (`oi4` to `oi6`, `oi10`, `oi12`, `oi13`, `oi16`, `hp1` to `hp5`, `mv1`, `mv3`, `ae4`, `ae5`, `sb6`),
// through a nested statement too (`oi18`, `oi19`, `oi35`). A refill after it hides nothing (`hq1` to `hq1d`, `hq7`, `hr5`, `hr6`, `hr7`, `hs9`, `hs10`, `hs16`, `sb9`), nor does a `defer` that refills or frees (`hr5b` to `hr5f`, `hs1` to `hs7`, `hs11`, `hs13`, `hs14`, `hs17`).
// Assigning one by `=` or `$$m` is ASSIGN-005 unless it's an inline array or struct that can't drop (`type_may_drop`), since assigning or claiming one frees nothing: the address the target formed stays good, and a pointer or an index it read out of it keeps the value it had, by this order (a pointee a `wild` pointer in it names, freed by a callee, is DEF-579's): `ss10` is a fault that rule closes, a store into a page the value sealed and replaced, and
// `k3a`, `k3c`, `k3d`, `gk1`, `gk3b` and `mc5` are stores into a buffer the value freed. A `List` is `TY_STRUCT`, BORROW-015 sees a local holder and never a call's temporary, and `type_drops` alone says no at a `T` whose instance frees (`gk1`, in `target_generic_may_drop`). Through a macro the event is the expansion's (`mc1`, `mc2`, `mc3`, `mc5`).
// PRICES, right programs this refuses, each with one remedy, bind the value first: a kept scalar, pointer, string or slice assigned in the value (`hr3`, `hr4`, `hsc1`, `ss6`, `ae6`, `sa10`, `sc1`, `sc5`, `sc12`, `sx1d`, and `oi9e` in `compound_assignment_reads_its_name`);
// an aggregate that may drop, assigned whole in the value, whose store goes nowhere near what it holds (`ae2`, `ae8`, `sa12`), a generic's `Bx<T>` (`gk2`, in `target_generic_may_drop`), and an array past the predicate's fuel of 16 (`gk4b`, `gk3`);
// a free or move on a road that then jumps, so the store never runs (`hs12`, `hq13`, `hr2`); a kept name moved and refilled (`hq8`, `hq8b`, `ae9`). `hr5e` and `hs15` are refused on main too.
// DEF-575's cells are not here: the rule stands for what the value moves, frees or assigns BY NAME, and says nothing of `@l` handed to a callee in the value, a temporary pointer, or a holder of a struct or array holding a `List`.
// DEF-574's cells are not here: a `wild` name read as an operand, then freed and refilled by a later operand of one expression, needs no assignment, and a target's own window is one case of it.
mod:oe_asg_ix_val_p = {
error:E5_oe_asg_ix_val_p;
struct:H = { string:s; int64:k; };
func:mkh = H() never fails { pass H{ s: string_concat("ab", "cde"), k: 7i64 }; };
func:eath = int64(move H:v) never fails { pass 0i64; };
func:ok = int64() { pass 7i64; };
func:bad = int64() { fail E5_oe_asg_ix_val_p; };
func:okn = int64(int64:n) { if (n > 90i64) { fail E5_oe_asg_ix_val_p; } pass 7i64; };
struct:S2 = { int64:a; int64:b; };
struct:M = { int64:k; };
func:mm = int64(M:self, int64:v) never fails { pass self.k + v; };
func:two = int64(int64:a, int64:b) never fails { pass a + b; };
func:f = int64(int64:n) never fails {
    int64:out = 7i64;
    int64[4]:a = [0i64, 0i64, 0i64, 0i64];
    int64:cell = 0i64;
    int64->:pv = @cell;
    int64:y;
    int64:i = 0i64;
    lp: while (true) unbounded {
        i = i + 1i64;
        a[pick (n) { (1i64) { break lp; }, (*) { give 0i64; } }] = pick (n) { (*) { y = 7i64; give 1i64; } };
        if (i > 1i64) { break lp; }
    }
    out = y;
    discard(a[0i64]); discard(<-pv);
    pass out;
};
};
